## E-mail sent to a restricted Item's author when a user requests a copy.
  ##
  ## Parameters: 0 requester's name
  ## 1 requester's address
  ## 2 name of a single bitstream, or "all"
  ## 3 item Handle
  ## 4 item title
  ## 5 message from requester
  ## 6 link back to DSpace for action
  ## 7 corresponding author name
  ## 8 corresponding author email
  ## 9 configuration property "dspace.name"
  ## 10 configuration property "mail.helpdesk"
  #set($subject = 'Infoscience. request copy of document')
  
 Hello ${params[7]},
  
 A user of ${params[9]}, named ${params[0]} (${params[1]}), requested a copy of the file(s) associated with the document: "${params[4]}" (${params[3]}) submitted by you.
  
 The request came along with the following message:
 "${params[5]}"
  
 Whether you choose to approve or deny the request, we thank you to take the time to respond.
 To answer the user, click here: ${params[6]}. 
 
 If you are not an author of this document, but only submitted the document on the author's behalf, please redirect this message to the author(s).
 Only the author(s) is entitled to answer the request to send a copy.
  
 If your are not in a position to treat or redirect this request, or if you need further assistance, please contact us: ${params[10]}
  
 Thank you for your kind cooperation, EPFL supports any approach that promotes Open Science.
 
 Best regards,
 
 Infoscience Team
 EPFL Library
